Time Complexity

For every selected node, we may examine all other nodes.

O(N² log N)

where N = number of points.

Space Complexity
O(N²)

Priority Queue may contain many candidate edges.

Key Learning
MST can be applied even when edges are not explicitly given.
Manhattan Distance can act as edge weights.
Prim's Algorithm is useful for dense graphs.
Min Heap helps in selecting the minimum weight edge efficiently.
Solution (Prim's Algorithm)
class Solution {
public:
    int manhattanDist(vector<vector<int>>& points,int p1,int p2){
        return abs(points[p1][0]-points[p2][0]) +
               abs(points[p1][1]-points[p2][1]);
    }

    int minCostConnectPoints(vector<vector<int>>& points) {
        int n = points.size();

        priority_queue<
            pair<int,int>,
            vector<pair<int,int>>,
            greater<pair<int,int>>
        > pq;

        vector<bool> mstSet(n,false);

        int mst = 0;

        pq.push({0,0});

        while(!pq.empty()){
            auto p = pq.top();
            pq.pop();

            int wt = p.first;
            int node = p.second;

            if(mstSet[node]) continue;

            mstSet[node] = true;
            mst += wt;

            for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
                if(!mstSet[i]){
                    int edgeWt = manhattanDist(points,node,i);
                    pq.push({edgeWt,i});
                }
            }
        }

        return mst;
    }
};
